Because it carries no key, nothing can cancel it. Every other animation in the file is keyed precisely so it *can* be cancelled (`"appearFade"`, `"appearScale"`, `"layoutMove"`, `"focusMove"`, `"focusFade"`, `"lineDrawAnimation"`), and `grep -n "removeAllActions\|removeAction(forKey" PresenceNetworkScene.swift` returns hits only for those keys (lines 601, 1063, 1073, 1100, 1107, 1283, 1300, 1309, 1365) — never for the disappearance sequence.

