```
called unconditionally from LoggingDetailView.swift:131-140 `.task { ... await capture.loadHistoricalLogs(from: dir) }`, from the Refresh button at LoggingDetailView.swift:250-252, and from the arbitrary-folder import at LoggingDetailView.swift:601 `Task { await capture.importFromDirectory(url) }` → DittoLogCaptureService.swift:167 `LogFileParser.parseDirectory(url)`. `LoggingDetailView()` is unguarded in MainStudioView.swift:330-331 (`case .logging:`) — the `#if os(iOS)` there only attaches a toolbar, so iPadOS runs the same path.

`.log.gz` is the real on-disk format, not hypothetical: `~/Library/Application Support/DittoEdgeStudio/quickstarts-.../ditto_logs/` holds 12 rotated `*.log.gz` files (935 KB compressed, ISIZE 19,999,667 — a 20x ratio, so the intact path relies entirely on ISIZE being honest).

Measured, not assumed. Truncating one real archive at 19 points and reading the resulting last-4-bytes as LE UInt32 gives buffer sizes with mean 1.87 GiB and max 3.76 GiB (e.g. 65% → 4,038,976,470 bytes). And the allocation is committed, not lazy: `/usr/bin/time -l` on `[UInt8](repeating: 0, count: 2_600_966_635)` reports `2654046680 peak memory footprint` — the full 2.47 GiB is resident, which is a jetsam kill on iPadOS and a multi-GB stall on macOS.
